    "title": "Mark Consuelos Reveals His Dad Recently Passed Away ‘Peacefully,’ Kelly Ripa Calls Him ‘The Greatest’",
    "text": "Mark Consuelos is opening up about his family’s heartbreaking loss.During the Monday, April 6, episode of Live with Kelly and Mark, per People, the 55-year-old revealed that his father, Saul Consuelos, died on March 23 after a long illness.“He passed away peacefully,” Mark said, reflecting on his father’s final days.Mark’s wife Kelly Ripa paid a touching tribute to her father-in-law, describing him as “the greatest person I’ve ever known” and adding that she will miss him “every day for the rest of my life.”The couple’s three children — Michael, 28, Lola, 24, and Joaquin, 23 — are also grieving deeply, with Ripa, 55, noting this is their first experience losing a loved one.Mark remembered his father as a hardworking and devoted man who immigrated from Mexico as a teenager and went on to serve in the U.S. Navy for 30 years.“He loved his country so much,” he said, praising his dad’s dedication and resilience.Valerie Goodloe/MediaPunch / MEGAMark also reflected on the life lessons his father passed down, recalling how he learned how to fix things around the house by watching Saul.Now, the family is focused on supporting Mark’s mother, Camilla, in the wake of losing their beloved patriarch. “We gotta take care of mom. We’re trying to convince my mom to move to New York,” Mark said. “She’s such a character, she’s stubborn.”Turning to Ripa, he asked: “What do you think, a cooking segment here on Fridays with Camilla?”“Yeah! Cooking with Camilla! Put her to work!” Ripa quipped. “Enough of this life of leisure!”Read More From InTouch WeeklyThis story Mark Consuelos Reveals His Dad Recently Passed Away ‘Peacefully,’ Kelly Ripa Calls Him ‘The Greatest’ first appeared on InTouch Weekly. Add InTouch Weekly as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
